Package: drzreplay
Version: @VERSION@
Architecture: all
Maintainer: upidddd <189487697+upidddd@users.noreply.github.com>
Installed-Size: @SIZE@
Depends: python3 (>= 3.11), python3-gi, gir1.2-gtk-4.0, gir1.2-adw-1 (>= 1.5), ffmpeg, libx11-6, x11-xserver-utils, pulseaudio-utils, libnotify-bin, xdg-utils
Recommends: gir1.2-gtk-3.0, gir1.2-ayatanaappindicator3-0.1, xdg-user-dirs, dunst | notification-daemon,
 xdg-desktop-portal, gstreamer1.0-pipewire, gstreamer1.0-plugins-good, gstreamer1.0-plugins-bad,
 gstreamer1.0-plugins-ugly, gstreamer1.0-libav, gstreamer1.0-tools, libgtk-4-media-gstreamer
Section: video
Priority: optional
Description: instant replay recorder for Linux (X11 and Wayland)
 DrzReplay keeps the last minute of your screen and sound in memory and saves
 it to a video file when you press a hotkey (Alt+Z by default) — like
 "instant replay" in game overlays. Clips can open with a short animated
 metal-gate intro (off by default).
 .
 Video is encoded on the graphics card (NVIDIA NVENC or AMD/Intel VA-API,
 CPU x264 as a fallback) and buffered in RAM, so games stay smooth.
 Includes a settings app, tray icon and global hotkey for X11 desktops
 (including tiling window managers such as i3) and Wayland (GNOME, KDE).
